**Memorandum**

**To:** Train Operations Division  
**From:** Sarah Johnson, Operations Manager  
**Date:** April 15, 2024  
**Subject:** Upcoming Freight Scheduling and Infrastructure Updates  

As we approach the third quarter of 2024, it is imperative that we optimize our freight train scheduling to enhance service efficiency across our network. Effective May 1, 2024, the North Central Division will implement a new scheduling protocol developed in collaboration with the Freight Scheduling Department and the Data Analytics Team at TranzRail Systems. This initiative aims to reduce idle time at key junctions, particularly at the Denver Union Station and the Kansas City Intermodal Facility. 

Our partnership with Horizon Logistics will facilitate the coordination of freight loads, ensuring that we can meet the increased demand projected by the National Freight Transportation Report, which estimates a 15% rise in freight activity by the end of Q3. Additionally, our recent investment in the Enhanced Rail Infrastructure Program, specifically the upgrades to the 152-mile stretch of track between Omaha and Lincoln, will improve transit times by an estimated 30 minutes per trip, positively impacting our delivery schedules.

The Operations Control Center will oversee the integration of new scheduling software, RailSync 3.0, which is designed to streamline communication between train crews, maintenance teams, and dispatchers. This system will enhance real-time tracking of our fleet, particularly the 200 freight cars managed by the Central Freight Lines. We expect to see a 20% reduction in delays associated with track maintenance due to the predictive analytics features of RailSync 3.0.

Please ensure that all team members are briefed on these changes by April 25, 2024. The Training Department will provide additional resources to assist in this transition. Your cooperation is crucial as we aim to deliver on our commitment to efficiency and reliability, thereby enhancing our customer satisfaction ratings with major clients such as Best Buy and Amazon, who rely heavily on our punctual service.

Should you have any questions or require further details, please do not hesitate to reach out.

Best,  
Sarah Johnson  
Operations Manager  
